language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Find an auto-referential series S = (s_0, ..., s_{n+1}) where s_i counts the occurrences of i in S, for i = 0..n, and s_{n+1} = m.
given n : int(1..)
given m : int(0..)
find s : matrix indexed by [int(1..n+2)] of int(0..n)
branching on [s]
such that
$ every entry of S is one of the counted values 0..n
forAll j : int(1..n+2) . s[j] <= n,
$ s_{n+1} equals m
s[n+2] = m,
$ for each i in 0..n, s_i is the number of occurrences of i in the series S
forAll i : int(0..n) . s[i+1] = (sum j : int(1..n+2) . (s[j] = i))
